
1. These fonts are generated by modifying  Hanyang fonts 
   available as hanfont.pcf.tar.gz at ftp://ftp.kaist.ac.kr.

2. Now, FONT_DESCENT has more reasonable values than in 
   original Hanyang fonts. Thus, spacing between lines
   are more reasonable than before.

3. These fonts are defined as 'character cell' fonts rather
   than 'monospace' fonts, so that you don't need to
   make alias to get them available in 'Options-General-
   Font-Proportional' menu in Netscape. 

4. Installation :

     - put all of pcf files in the directory you want to 
       install them

     - if your X server can handle compressed fonts, 
          compress them with 'compress'(not with 'gzip'). 

     - In that directory, run 

         $ mkfontdir . 
         $ xset fp `pwd`'
         $ xset fp rehash 

     - Note that these fonts have the same names as original 
       Hanyang fonts, so that you may have to eliminate
       lines for aliasing 'propotional' Hanyang fonts to 
       'monospace' fonts at the end of 'font.alias' file
       if you previously installed original Hanyang fonts

     - check if they're available for you to use

        $ xlsfonts | grep hanyang
        

5. Note for X11 R4 users

      - PCF fonts can be converted to SNF by getting 
        BDF with 'xbdfdump' on X11 R5 or R6 server  
        and converting BDF to SNF with 'bdftosnf'. 

    



